{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RU7MHw3GfpvNXEj8fM3E46","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tasks: new policy: playwright only if necessary\n2\t\n3\tid: prior\n4\tanalyst: analyst\n5\tdate: 2026-10-11\n6\t\n7\t<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n8\t\n9\t## Overview\n10\t\n11\tAdd one new global catalog policy under `policies/` capturing the brief's rule:\n12\tbrowser automation (Playwright, and the `shot` render path that drives it) is\n13\texpensive, so it should be reached for only when it is genuinely necessary or\n14\thelpful — static analysis and cheaper verification come first. This is a\n15\tcontent-only change: a single plain-markdown policy file, no frontmatter,\n16\tfollowing the format the `medical_policies` job established (one-line heading +\n17\tthe rule + at most a line or two of why; the filename is the identity).\n18\t\n19\tScope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n20\t- The deliverable is a **global catalog policy** at `policies/<name>.md` — the\n21\t  brief says \"create a new policy\", and this repo's source-of-truth policy\n22\t  directory is the top-level `policies/` (not `docs/policies/`, which is the\n23\t  per-project tier described in `docs/AGENTS.md`).\n24\t- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n25\t  `docs/` other than this job's own files.\n26\t- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — keep\n27\t  the directory to policy files only.\n28\t- Keep the file short: heading + rule + at most a line or two of why.\n29\t\n30\t## Framing note for @developer (important, not a blocker)\n31\t\n32\tThe `medical_policies` brief's decision criteria for a global catalog policy\n33\tare the real format spec here: a policy must be **universal** (true for every\n34\tproject/language/task) and must **not be situational or tool-specific** — if a\n35\trule is \"when doing X, …\", it belongs in a **skill** or a **project** policy,\n36\tnever a global catalog one. A rule named purely after one tool (`playwright`)\n37\treads as situational and would fail criterion 1/4.\n38\t\n39\tRecommended resolution: frame the policy around the **universal principle** —\n40\tprefer the cheapest sufficient verification; reserve slow/heavyweight tooling\n41\t(browser automation such as Playwright, or `shot` renders) for when static\n42\tanalysis, reading the code, or lighter tests genuinely cannot answer the\n43\tquestion — and name Playwright as the concrete motivating example rather than\n44\tthe whole subject. Suggested filename: `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md`\n45\t(the filename is the policy's identity and should stay recognisable).\n46\t\n47\tKnown tension to record (do **not** silently expand scope): `agents/developer.md`\n48\tlines ~107-129 instruct the developer to verify UI changes with `shot`, and\n49\t`agents/tester.md` line ~96 points at the `webapp-testing` skill (Playwright).\n50\tThe policy must **complement** those role instructions, not contradict them;\n51\tword it so it governs *when* to reach for the browser, leaving the existing\n52\t\"verify rendered UI work\" guidance intact. If a genuine contradiction cannot be\n53\tavoided without editing an agent file, stop and flag it in `implementation.md`\n54\trather than editing `agents/` (that is out of scope for this brief).\n55\t\n56\t## Task breakdown\n57\t\n58\t### TASK-1 — Author `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md`\n59\t\n60\t- **Description**: Create the global policy file carrying the brief's rule —\n61\t  browser automation / Playwright is a costly verification path, so use it only\n62\t  when it is strictly necessary or genuinely helpful; prefer static analysis and\n63\t  cheaper checks first. Write it as a short, universal, session-wide always/\n64\t  never constraint (heading + rule + a line of why), tool-neutral in spirit with\n65\t  Playwright named only as the motivating example.\n66\t- **Files**: `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md` (new)\n67\t- **Depends**: none\n68\t- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only; the only judgement call is the\n69\t  universal framing (see note above), not any code path.\n70\t\n71\t### TASK-2 — Audit the new policy against the existing catalog\n72\t\n73\t- **Description**: Check the new file against the `medical_policies` criteria\n74\t  and the catalog content that actually exists here: shorten wording if it\n75\t  exceeds a short rule, and confirm it (a) is universal, (b) adds scope rather\n76\t  than restating the `webapp-testing`/`frontend-design` skills or\n77\t  `prompts/meta.md`, and (c) does not contradict `agents/developer.md` (the\n78\t  `shot` render guidance) or `agents/tester.md` (Playwright via\n79\t  `webapp-testing`). Adjust the phrasing to resolve any conflict within the\n80\t  policy file; record the dedupe/consistency reasoning and any decision that\n81\t  cannot be made in-file in `implementation.md`.\n82\t- **Files**: `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md` (may be edited);\n83\t  `implementation.md` (record the outcome)\n84\t- **Depends**: TASK-1\n85\t- **Risk**: medium — a judgement-based pass that can change or trim the\n86\t  delivered wording, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n87\t  brief's criteria and the \"add scope, don't restate\" rule.\n88\t\n89\t## Notes / open questions\n90\t\n91\t- The brief's `Why`, `Out of scope`, and `Notes` sections are empty; the What is\n92\t  specific enough to proceed. No human decision was required. The main open\n93\t  design point — universal-principle framing vs. a Playwright-named rule — is\n94\t  resolved in favour of the universal framing above, because a situational rule\n95\t  does not qualify as a global catalog policy; if the reviewer disagrees, the\n96\t  alternative is a `docs/policies/` project rule or a skill, which is a larger\n97\t  decision than this brief describes.\n98\t- This repo has no build/test tooling; verification is content review against\n99\t  the policy format and criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n100\t- If a follow-up is ever wanted (e.g. softening `agents/developer.md`'s\n101\t  unconditional \"verify UI with shot\" wording), it is out of scope here and\n102\t  should be tracked as its own job.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b6b4c23-52e8-49de-a3c6-46cb22ff3ef2","uuid":"5a1968ae-ca6f-42d2-a4bf-ec176328e42b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:18:37.535Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/tasks.md","content":"# Tasks: new policy: playwright only if necessary\n\nid: prior\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd one new global catalog policy under `policies/` capturing the brief's rule:\nbrowser automation (Playwright, and the `shot` render path that drives it) is\nexpensive, so it should be reached for only when it is genuinely necessary or\nhelpful — static analysis and cheaper verification come first. This is a\ncontent-only change: a single plain-markdown policy file, no frontmatter,\nfollowing the format the `medical_policies` job established (one-line heading +\nthe rule + at most a line or two of why; the filename is the identity).\n\nScope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n- The deliverable is a **global catalog policy** at `policies/<name>.md` — the\n  brief says \"create a new policy\", and this repo's source-of-truth policy\n  directory is the top-level `policies/` (not `docs/policies/`, which is the\n  per-project tier described in `docs/AGENTS.md`).\n- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n  `docs/` other than this job's own files.\n- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — keep\n  the directory to policy files only.\n- Keep the file short: heading + rule + at most a line or two of why.\n\n## Framing note for @developer (important, 