{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018THzo1tbQNT1n2Xq5sfd88","type":"tool_result","content":"# Implementation: don't be lazy policy\n\nid: piece\ndeveloper:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->\n\n## Changes\n\n<!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n<!-- Anything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope but should be tracked. -->\n# Verdict: don't be lazy policy\n\nid: piece\nreviewer:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\n<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n     notes: ...\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n\n## Security\n\n<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n\n## Overall\n\n<!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n<!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->\n5a30f1a [piece] chore: commit all\n345ac2b [piece] chore: commit all\nb9fdc38 Scaffold job piece_don-t-be-lazy-policy\n0253e76 Create report skill\nc1925cd Merge branch 'main' of github.com:lmuskalla/manigot-catalog\nc91210f new policy: playwright only if necessary\ncf1dba8 added: backlog-entry skill\n14cdd54 chore: stop tracking .manigot\nask-before-adding-dependencies.md\nkeep-it-committed.md\nno-debug-leftovers.md\nplaywright-only-if-necessary.md\nsecrets-hygiene.md\n== policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md\n# Ask before adding dependencies\n\nDo not add a dependency without explicit approval.\nA new dependency is a lasting cost to the whole project, so surface the need\nand let a human decide.\n== policies/keep-it-committed.md\n# Keep it committed\n\nLeave no uncommitted work behind.\nRecord changes in the project before finishing so nothing is lost or left in\nan ambiguous half-finished state.\n== policies/no-debug-leftovers.md\n# No debug leftovers\n\nLeave no debug output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO without a\ntracked issue behind.\nRemove them before finishing so the change ships only what it needs.\n== policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md\n# Browser automation only if necessary\n\nPrefer static analysis, reading the code, or a lighter test over browser\nautomation; reach for Playwright (or a `shot` render) only when those cannot\nanswer the question.\nDriving a browser is slow and costly, so it should be the exception, not the\ndefault.\n== policies/secrets-hygiene.md\n# Secrets hygiene\n\nNever commit, log, print, or hardcode secrets, tokens, keys, or credentials.\nRead them from the environment or untracked config, and keep them out of\nsource, diffs, command output, and error messages.\n# manigot — system-wide meta prompt\n\nThis is the system-wide layer: general character and goals that apply to\nevery session. Your agent file and the project context remain the operative\nper-role instructions.\n\n## Character\n\n- Be a careful, senior engineer. Prefer small, focused, well-understood\n  changes over broad sweeping ones. When scope is unclear, ask rather than\n  guess — never silently expand a task.\n- Prefer concrete verification over assumption: build, run, and inspect\n  actual output wherever you can.\n- Be friendly, assume you are dumber than the person you are talking to and make sure not to be condescending. It is most likely you know less than the user.\n- Don't do things you're not asked to do.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55d251eb-a762-4104-8a88-77c2c3cbfa06","uuid":"b933b8cd-683e-4fb2-87e8-b7e275146910","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:19:08.959Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Implementation: don't be lazy policy\n\nid: piece\ndeveloper:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->\n\n## Changes\n\n<!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->\n\n## Known 